<title>UK: POLL-FX Analytics wins July Reuters forex poll.</title>
<headline>POLL-FX Analytics wins July Reuters forex poll.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>FX Analytics in New York won the Reuters  July foreign exchange poll, beating 30 other banks and financial institutions  around the world.</p>
<p>FX Analytics predicted the dollar at 1.7700 marks and 117.50 yen and  sterling at 1.6400 dollars at end-July. The average divergence in  the FX Analytics forecasts from the London closing levels on July  31 was just 1.53 percent.</p>
<p>On July 31, dollar/mark closed at 1.8390, dollar/yen at 118.50 and  sterling/dollar at 1.6400.</p>
<p>Bank of Montreal, Toronto came second with a divergence of 2.14 percent,  followed by UBS in London with a divergence of 2.54 percent.</p>
<p>Percentage differences in the poll between forecast and actual levels  varied between 1.53 percent and 5.61 percent.</p>
